emoved","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:0b177ddc3c05d5e9d6a6686fae963a5932bcf56c3e380238226bf37e4870339c","file":"preprints/Bochner-Riesz-Multipliers-in-Three-Dimensions-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":21,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"8f96a7865e387ea9b2178d92fd3992f4ce5fbb2328b9a163c4e6ad0b262d40a0","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Bochner-Riesz-Multipliers-in-Three-Dimensions-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:0b177ddc3c05d5e9d6a6686fae963a5932bcf56c3e380238226bf37e4870339c","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Bochner-Riesz-Multipliers-in-Three-Dimensions-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L21"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:bochner-riesz}\nFor every $\\delta>0$, there is a finite constant $C_\\delta$ such that\n\\begin{equation}\n \\norm{T_\\delta f}_{L^3(\\RR^3)}\n \\le C_\\delta\\norm f_{L^3(\\RR^3)}\n \\qquad(f\\in\\mathcal S(\\RR^3)).\n \\label{eq:main-bound}\n\\end{equation}\nConsequently $T_\\delta$ has a unique bounded extension to $L^3(\\RR^3)$."}
